# .env for zedu-mobile PR builds in contributor forks (pr-build-react-native.yml).
# Read at the zedu-ci commit the caller pins, so a change ships with a caller bump.
# Public values only: everything here is bundled into the app,
# so anyone with a build can read it. Never add a secret.
#
# {{backend}} is the API host: api.zedu.chat (the live backend), or the host from the PR
# body's `Backend URL:` line. {{client}} is the matching web app host (the backend host without "api.").
# Keys the app reads are declared in zedu-mobile's env.d.ts. GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, CLIENT_ID,
# CLIENT_SECRET and AGORA_APP_ID stay unset, as in zedu-fe's previews: Google sign-in and calls don't
# work in review builds. ONESIGNAL_APP_ID can't stay unset: the app calls OneSignal.initialize at
# startup, and a null app id aborts native init (NullPointerException in OneSignal.initWithContext),
# so the release build crashes on launch. The all-zero id is not a real OneSignal app: init succeeds
# and push never arrives.
API_URL=https://{{backend}}
BASE_URL=https://{{backend}}/api/v1
CONNECT_URL=wss://{{backend}}/centrifugo/connection/websocket
CLIENT_URL=https://{{client}}
ONESIGNAL_APP_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
